y by  6 so we'll also multiply the numerator  by 6.  and we see one half and six twelfths  these are the same thing one is one is  half of two six is half of twelve  and how would we write eleven twelfths  as something over twelve  well it's already written as something  over twelve eleven twelfths already has  twelve in the denominator so we don't  have to change that  eleven twelfths and now we're ready to  add  so this is going to be equal to  six  this is going to be equal to six  plus  11  6 plus  11  over 12  over 12. we have 6 12  plus 11 12 is going to be 6 plus 11  over 12.  which is equal to 6 plus 11 is 17  12. if we want to write it as a mixed  number that is what 12 goes into 17 one  time with a remainder 5. so 1 and 5  over 12.  let's do one more of these this is this  is strangely fun  all right let's say that we wanted to  add  we're going to add 3  4  2  we're going to add 3 fourths  to  one fifth  two one  over five what is this going to be and  once again pause the video and see if  you can work it out  well we have different denominators here  and we wanna find this we want to  rewrite these so they have the same  denominator so we have to find a common  multiple ideally the least common  multiple so what's the least common  multiple of four and five  we'll start with the larger number and  let's look at its multiples and and keep  increasing them until we get one that's  divisible by four  so five is not divisible by four  ten is not divisible by four  or perfectly divisible by four is what  we care about fifteen is not perfectly  divisible by four twenty is divisible by  4 in fact that is 5 times 4 that is 20.  so what we could do is we could write  both of these fractions as having 20 in  the denominator or 20 as a denominator  so we could write 3 4 is something over  20.  so to go from 4 to 20 in the denominator  we multiplied by 5. so we also do that  to the numerator we multiplied 3 times 5  to get 15.  all i did to go from 4 to 20 multiply